cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "UMAT-OTI: Deterministic operational-Taylor tangent generation for Abaqus UMATs"
abstract: >-
  UMAT-OTI transforms Abaqus user-material subroutine (UMAT) Fortran source so
  that the consistent material tangent (DDSDDE) is computed by operational-Taylor
  (OTI) automatic differentiation instead of hand-coded or finite-difference
  derivatives, driven by a compact JSON contract.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/santiagarcia/UMAT_source_transformation"
url: "https://github.com/santiagarcia/UMAT_source_transformation"
keywords:
  - Abaqus
  - UMAT
  - automatic differentiation
  - operational Taylor integration
  - consistent tangent
  - finite element method
  - constitutive models
